    "summary": "High‑energy Manor Downs ’82 with killer Scarlet>Fire and soaring Morning Dew",
    "review": "The July 31, 1982 Manor Downs show is a quintessential early‑’80s Dead romp – the band rides a wave of pure, unbridled energy from the opening Alabama Getaway all the way through an incendiary encore. Highlights abound: a monster Scarlet Begonias → Fire on the Mountain that still smokes, razor‑sharp Estimated Prophet → Eyes of the World segues, and a soaring, emotional Morning Dew that caps the second set. Candyman, Bird Song, Deal and a raucous One More Saturday Night keep the momentum rolling, while the seamless Uncle John’s Band → Truckin' transition adds that extra spark. Across all sources the performance feels locked‑in, with Brent Mydland’s keyboards adding rich texture, Bill & Mickey hammering out a thunderous dual‑drum groove, and Jerry delivering crisp, birthday‑fuelled leads.",
